          "worked": "The Yes sector is larger than a semicircle, so its percentage must exceed $50\\%$; $43\\%$ is too low. The No sector covers about two fifths of the circle, or about $40\\%$, so $47\\%$ is too high. Together the two categories cover all staff, but $43\\%+47\\%=90\\%$, leaving $10\\%$ unaccounted for.",
